{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1449596-house-liam\u2019s-crest","id":1449596,"title":"House Liam\u2019s crest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-25T18:26:51-07:00","id":1449596,"title":"House Liam\u2019s crest?","content":"Ok, after all these years I am going to ask the question: why does House Liam have a dead tree as it\u2019s heraldry? I can understand the OTHER noble houses feeling the symbol is appropriate, but why do the Liam sidhe put up with it? Was King Liam just feeling depressed, or should we assume there is a story behind it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T19:32:34-07:00","id":1449605,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming might enforce the image. Unwholesome and unfair ideas are often enforced by the Dreaming. Maybe Commoners need to seek influence in Hollywood and alter the Dreaming through film and TV. Certainly it looks like the Nobles did. Take Star Trek as an example. I can't think of a single episode of the sixties series that delt with monarchs or monarchies that had a positive or neutral view of monarchy. By the time ST: tNG rolled around was there a single episode dealing with monarchies that didn't take a positive view of monarchies? King's used to be the villains or fools in everything but swashbucklers (the Yul Brenner &quot;King and I&quot; is the major exception). Look at &quot;Anna and the King of Siam&quot; the non-musical Rex Harrison treatment of the story, the King is scarier and far less sympathetic. Even in most Swashbucklers kings are normally fools or villains. Certain rare individuals are excepted. But even Elizabeth Tudor, normally heroic or at least sympathetic, is depicted as an out and out villain in several films. Is that even imaginable today? <br /> <br /> Moreover, can you remember a single treatment of a president of an American nation depicted as a villain before 1965? Hollywood even did a hagiography of Jurez! Could you imagine a film made in the present period in Hollywood set in the early federal period that would depict Washington or Jefferson as even honest or decent men?<br /> Hollywood is owned by the Nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:07:40-07:00","id":1449924,"title":"","content":"The Liam are a house fallen into disrepute for a supposedly broken Oath...<br /> Or maybe just because they like humans so very much.<br /> <br /> At any rate, perhaps they keep the dead tree as a symbol that someday they might bloom again<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}